    {
      "id": 185452,
      "name": "dpt",
      "username": "dpt",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/dpt/{size}/1922_2.png",
      "created_at": "2016-11-27T02:22:10.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Spiff\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/spiff/48/1865_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Spiff:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Is the same Fireside Chat topic updated whenever there's something new added, or is there a new one added each time there's a new set of info?</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>There's one Fireside Chat post that keeps getting updated. (Hmm, I'm surprised the forum bug on editing posts hasn't been more of an issue there.)</p>\n<p>But they do it in a kind of friendly way, in that each new set of updates gets added at the end of the post, marked off by dividers. It looks like when an earlier ruling is updated, they add a specific note to that effect. Search for 'Ammo' for an example. So it shouldn't be too hard to keep things up-to-date.</p>",
